@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.security"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Product Bundle Admin Permissions
	Testing to assure that provisioning product bundle admin permissions works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I create a provisioning user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | provisioning.admin                    |
	| Email Address | provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Provisioning                          |
	| Last Name     | Admin                                 |
	* I assign the provisioning user with the email address "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" to the provisioning role "Provisioning Admin"

Teardown:
	* I log out and log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	* I go to the product bundles index page
	* I tear down the following product bundles
	| Visible Products |
	| Changed Products |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Visible Product        |
	| A Visible Second Product |
	| A Visible Third Product  |
	| A Visible Fourth Product |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: Create product bundle
	Testing the ability to create product bundles in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible Second Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Visible Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Visible Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Visible Second Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Visible Products" and the following values
	| Name | Visible Products |
	When I click on the product bundle with the name "Visible Products" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product "A Visible Product" on the product bundle
	And I should be able to view the product "A Visible Second Product" on the product bundle

Scenario: Update product bundle
	Testing the ability to update product bundles in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible Second Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible Third Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible Fourth Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Visible Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Visible Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Visible Second Product |
	And I click on the product bundle with the name "Visible Products" on the provisioning index
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name           | Input | Changed Products         |
	| Remove Product |       | A Visible Second Product |
	| Add Product    |       | A Visible Third Product  |
	| Remove Product |       | A Visible Product        |
	| Add Product    |       | A Visible Fourth Product |
	Then I should be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Changed Products" and the following values
	| Name | Changed Products |
	And I should not be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Visible Products"
	When I click on the product bundle with the name "Changed Products" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product "A Visible Third Product" on the product bundle
	And I should be able to view the product "A Visible Fourth Product" on the product bundle
	And I should not be able to view the product "A Visible Product" on the product bundle
	And I should not be able to view the product "A Visible Second Product" on the product bundle

Scenario: Delete product bundle
	Testing the ability to delete product bundles in the provisioning product index 

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible Product | |
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible Second Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the product bundles index page
	And I click on the new product bundle button
	And I populate and save the product bundle form with the following values
	| Name        | Input | Visible Products         |
	| Add Product |       | A Visible Product        |
	| Add Product |       | A Visible Second Product |
	And I click on the delete button for the product bundle "Visible Products"
	Then I should not be able to view a product bundle on the provisioning index with the name "Visible Products"